From: Jonas <sunjaroa@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [cmake] no ARM runtime CPU detection with MinGW

armcpu.c only implements the Windows ARM CPU check for MSVC (__try/__emit), so
MinGW builds stopped at its #error. Without the runtime check the NEON code is
still used when OPUS_PRESUME_NEON is set, which it is on AArch64.
---
 cmake/OpusFunctions.cmake | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/OpusFunctions.cmake b/cmake/OpusFunctions.cmake
--- a/cmake/OpusFunctions.cmake
+++ b/cmake/OpusFunctions.cmake
@@ -167,7 +167,10 @@ function(opus_supports_cpu_detection RUNTIME_CPU_CAPABILITY_DETECTION)
   elseif(OPUS_CPU_ARM)
     # ARM cpu detection is implemented for Windows, Linux, Android, FreeBSD
     # and OpenBSD.
-    if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "(Windows|Linux|Android|FreeBSD|OpenBSD)")
+    # On Windows only for MSVC: armcpu.c has no MinGW implementation.
+    if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Windows" AND NOT MSVC)
+      set(RUNTIME_CPU_CAPABILITY_DETECTION 0 PARENT_SCOPE)
+    elseif (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "(Windows|Linux|Android|FreeBSD|OpenBSD)")
       set(RUNTIME_CPU_CAPABILITY_DETECTION 1 PARENT_SCOPE)
     endif ()
   else()
